    "description": "Valley Cold Storage & Transportation provides temperature-controlled warehousing and related logistics services in southern New Mexico. Its customers include food, agriculture, food-service, and distribution businesses that need short- and long-term refrigerated storage near the U.S.-Mexico border. The business follows an asset-heavy operating model built around refrigerated warehouse infrastructure and associated transportation support rather than a brokered logistics model. Public company materials describe two strategically located facilities along the I-10 and I-25 corridors serving southern New Mexico, northern Mexico, and west Texas. Valley Cold's website identifies 2020 as the year of the current operating platform's launch, and Ridgewood Infrastructure acquired the company in 2024.",
